@*
    Its content as it was last drawn, until what it is drawn from changes.

    **For a part of a view that costs a lot to draw and seldom changes**, inside a component that renders all
    the time. Blazor builds a component's whole markup on every render, and a child handed a fragment is built
    again with it - a fragment is never the same parameter twice - so this decides for itself: it draws when the
    stamp it is handed differs from the one it last drew with, and keeps what it drew otherwise. The stamp has
    to say everything the content shows. Whatever it leaves out is what goes stale.

    The handlers it keeps are the ones it last drew with, and they go on working: they belong to the component
    the fragment came from, so a press on one renders that component, which hands this a new stamp - and the
    content is drawn again if the stamp says so.
*@
@ChildContent

@code {
    [Parameter]
    public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }

    ///<summary>Everything the content is drawn from, as one string. A different one draws it again.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string Stamp { get; set; } = "";

    private string drawnWith = "";

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        //The first render is never asked about, so the stamp it draws with is taken here.
        drawnWith = Stamp;
    }

    protected override bool ShouldRender()
    {
        if (Stamp == drawnWith)
            return false;

        drawnWith = Stamp;

        return true;
    }
}
